there is no newspaper of general circulation, the notice of intention must be posted in at least 3 public places within the jurisdiction.\n\nThis bill would require the proponents’ signatures and the street numbers and street names of their residence to be redacted or otherwise excluded from the notice of intention before it is made available to the public. If there is no newspaper of general circulation in the jurisdiction of the officer sought to be recalled, the bill would require the notice of intention to also be posted on at least 3 internet websites.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_enacted","date":null,"note":"Not enacted. The official status is \"Died\"."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-sb270","identifier":"SB 270","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"NO","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"MAJORITY"},"introducedDate":"2025-02-03","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Recall elections: notice of intention.","ruleId":"tag-direct-4","tag":"direct-democracy"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2026-02-02","lastActionText":"Returned to Secretary of Senate pursuant to Joint Rule 56.","lastCheckedAt":"2026-11-22T17:54:55Z","leadAuthors":"Introduced by Senator Ochoa Bogh; (Coauthors: Senators Choi, Hurtado, Jones, and Niello)","legislativeStatus":{"currentHouse":"Senate","currentLocation":"CS61","currentStatus":"Died","measureState":"Amended Senate"},"legislativeSubjects":[],"measureType":"Senate Bill","officialUrl":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260SB270","policyArea":null,"relatedMeasures":[],"selection":{"matched